{%- comment -%}
  Free-shipping progress bar for the cart drawer.

  A labelled progress bar showing how close the cart is to free shipping,
  counted in BOXES (not £) so a discount code can never pull the cart back
  under the threshold. Two states: a goal prompt ("buy two boxes" / "buy
  another box" once one is in, partial fill) and "unlocked" (full fill +
  success message), pluralised on boxes-needed.
  Pure Liquid — it reads cart.item_count and is re-rendered
  on every cart change because it lives inside the drawer's [data-drawer-body],
  which cart-drawer.js swaps via the Section Rendering API. No client JS.

  IMPORTANT: Shopify does not expose an automatic discount's threshold to Liquid
  (free-shipping discounts are shipping-level, applied at checkout). So
  `threshold` must be mirrored here from the discount config — the two can drift
  if only one is changed. The matching discount rule is "minimum quantity of
  items" = the same number.

  Basis: every cart line is a box (a pre-made box, or a "Build Your Box" line
  whose quantity is the number of identical boxes), so boxes = cart.item_count,
  which is also what a minimum-quantity discount counts. This holds for the
  current 4-pack range only: if loose single packs (the per-blend v2 builder)
  ever land in the cart as their own lines, item_count counts packs, not boxes,
  and this needs revisiting alongside the discount rule.

  Owned by sections/cart-drawer.liquid.

  Expects:
    - threshold: number of boxes that unlocks free shipping (e.g. 2). Bar is
      hidden when blank or <= 0.

  Usage:
    {% render 'cart-shipping-progress', threshold: section.settings.free_shipping_boxes %}
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign boxes_goal = threshold | round
  assign boxes_in_cart = cart.item_count

  assign qualified = false
  if boxes_goal > 0 and boxes_in_cart >= boxes_goal
    assign qualified = true
  endif

  # Boxes still needed for the "buy another box" / "buy two boxes" copy.
  # Always >= 1 in the unqualified branch.
  assign boxes_needed = boxes_goal | minus: boxes_in_cart

  assign percent = 0
  if boxes_goal > 0
    assign percent = boxes_in_cart | times: 100.00 | divided_by: boxes_goal
    if percent > 100
      assign percent = 100
    endif
  endif
  assign percent_aria = percent | round
-%}

{%- if boxes_goal > 0 -%}
  <div class="cart-shipping-progress{% if qualified %} is-qualified{% endif %}">
    <p class="cart-shipping-progress-message text-ui">
      {%- if qualified -%}
        {{ 'cart.drawer.shipping_progress_qualified' | t }}
      {%- else -%}
        {{ 'cart.drawer.shipping_progress_remaining' | t: count: boxes_needed }}
      {%- endif -%}
    </p>
    <div
      class="cart-shipping-progress-track"
      role="progressbar"
      aria-valuemin="0"
      aria-valuemax="100"
      aria-valuenow="{{ percent_aria }}"
      aria-label="{{ 'cart.drawer.shipping_progress_label' | t }}"
    >
      <div class="cart-shipping-progress-fill" style="--fill: {{ percent }}%;"></div>
    </div>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

{% stylesheet %}
  .cart-shipping-progress {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--spacing-xxs);
    padding: var(--spacing-xs);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .cart-shipping-progress-message {
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .cart-shipping-progress.is-qualified .cart-shipping-progress-message {
    color: #479d28;
  }

  .cart-shipping-progress-track {
    height: 6px;
    border-radius: var(--rad-s);
    background: var(--color-border);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  /* Width animates via transition (not @keyframes) so a cart update slides the
     fill from its current position to the new target. cart-drawer.js carries
     the outgoing width onto the freshly-swapped element to make that work — a
     bare transition alone can't, because the body innerHTML swap mounts a new
     fill node each refresh. */
  .cart-shipping-progress-fill {
    height: 100%;
    width: var(--fill);
    border-radius: inherit;
    background: var(--color-accent);
    transition: width var(--transition-slow);
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .cart-shipping-progress-fill {
      transition: none;
    }
  }
{% endstylesheet %}
